@node Common description
@chapter Description of the TGALoader library

TGALoader is a lightweight library for TGA images manipulation. Here are main
capabilities and restrictions of this library.

@itemize +
  @item Load TGA uncompressed images.
  @item Extract TGA header.
  @item Can flip image vertically for OpenGL usage.
  @item Can save RGB/RGBA images.
  @item Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v3 (LGPLv3).
@end itemize

@itemize @minus
  @item Can not load palette images.
  @item Can not load RLE compressed images.
  @item Can not read X-TARGA additional fields.
@end itemize

The main purpose of this library is to give simple interface to load textures
and images for OpenGL-based applications. It is also can be used to save
OpenGL framebuffer for debug purposes.

@node Library interface
@chapter Library interface

There are some new types, that defined by this library.

@deftp {Data type} tga_error_t
This type is an enumerator for all TGALoader error codes. Here is the table of
values such type variable can have:

@float table,table:tga_error_t
  @caption{Values of @code{tga_error_t} type}
  @multitable @columnfractions 0.5 0.5
    @headitem Name @tab Description
    @item @code{TGA_ERROR_OK} @tab 0 - No error.
    @item @code{TGA_ERROR_NO_SUCH_FILE} @tab TGA file is missing or can not
          be read.
    @item @code{TGA_ERROR_NOT_TGA} @tab File or stream is not a TGA image.
    @item @code{TGA_ERROR_MALLOC} @tab Can not allocate memory.
    @item @code{TGA_ERROR_EMPTY_IMAGE} @tab Image is empty, i.e. there is no
          image data.
    @item @code{TGA_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED} @tab TGA format not supported by
          this version.
  @end multitable
@end float
@end deftp

@deftp {Data type} tga_header_t
This type will contains TGA file header when TGA image will be loaded. Here
it's fields:

  @float table,table:tga_header_t
    @caption{@code{tga_header_t} structure fields}
    @multitable @columnfractions 0.4 0.2 0.4
      @headitem Name @tab Type @tab Description
      @item @code{id_length} @tab @code{uint8_t} @tab Length of the TGA image
            description string.
      @item @code{color_map_type} @tab @code{uint8_t} @tab Color type. Can be
            one of @code{tga_color_map_type_t} values.
      @item @code{image_type} @tab @code{uint8_t} @tab Image map type. Can be
            one of @code{tga_image_type_t} values.
      @item @code{color_map_specification} @tab @code{tga_color_map_t} @tab
            Color map descriptor. Has @code{tga_color_map_t} type.
      @item @code{image_type_specification} @tab @code{tga_image_t} @tab Image
            type descriptor. Has @code{tga_image_t} type.
    @end multitable
  @end float
@end deftp

@deftp {Data type} tga_color_map_type_t
This type describes the color map of the TGA image. It can have one of the
follows values:

  @float table,table:tga_color_map_type_t
    @caption{Values of @code{tga_color_map_type_t} type}
    @multitable @columnfractions 0.5 0.5
      @headitem Name @tab Description
      @item @code{TGA_NO_COLOR_MAP} @tab There is no colom map.
      @item @code{TGA_HAS_COLOR_MAP} @tab Color map is exists.
    @end multitable
  @end float
@end deftp

@deftp {Data type} tga_image_type_t
This type describes the image type of the TGA image, and can hold one of
values below:

  @float table,table:tga_image_type_t
    @caption{Values of @code{tga_image_type_t} type}
    @multitable @columnfractions 0.5 0.5
      @headitem Name @tab Description
      @item @code{TGA_NO_IMAGE} @tab TGA has no image (why this value can be
            used?)
      @item @code{TGA_IMAGE_COLOR_MAPPED} @tab Color mapped image data.
      @item @code{TGA_IMAGE_TRUECOLOR} @tab True color image data (RGB).
      @item @code{TGA_IMAGE_GRAYSCALE} @tab Grayscale image data.
      @item @code{TGA_IMAGE_RLE_COLOR_MAPPED} @tab Color mapped image data with
            RLE compression.
      @item @code{TGA_IMAGE_RLE_TRUECOLOR} @tab True color image data with RLE
            compression.
      @item @code{TGA_IMAGE_RLE_GRAYSCALE} @tab Grayscale image data with RLE
            compression.
    @end multitable
  @end float
@end deftp

@deftp {Data type} tga_color_map_t
This is the color map description structure.

  @float table,table:tga_color_map_t
    @caption{@code{tga_color_map_t} structure fields}
    @multitable @columnfractions 0.3 0.2 0.5
      @headitem Name @tab Type @tab Description
      @item @code{first_entry_index} @tab @code{uint16_t} @tab Index of the
            first entry in color map table.
      @item @code{color_map_length} @tab @code{uint16_t} @tab Number of the
            entries in color map table.
      @item @code{color_map_entry_size} @tab @code{uint8_t} @tab Size of the
            color map entry.
    @end multitable
  @end float
@end deftp

@deftp {Data type} tga_image_t
This is the image description structure.

  @float table,table:tga_image_t
    @caption{@code{tga_image_t} structure fields}
    @multitable @columnfractions 0.25 0.25 0.5
      @headitem Name @tab Type @tab Description
      @item @code{x_origin} @tab @code{uint16_t} @tab X origin position in the
            image.
      @item @code{y_origin} @tab @code{uint16_t} @tab Y origin position in the
            image.
      @item @code{width} @tab @code{uint16_t} @tab Width of the image.
      @item @code{height} @tab @code{uint16_t} @tab Height of the image.
      @item @code{pixel_depth} @tab @code{uint8_t} @tab Number of bits in the
            pixel.
      @item @code{image_descriptor} @tab @code{uint8_t} @tab Some additional
            bitfields of image descriptor.
    @end multitable
  @end float
@end deftp

The TGALoader has function interface bellow.

@deftypefun tga_error_t LoadTGAFromArray (const uint8_t* @code{raw_data}, size_t @code{length}, tga_header_t* @code{header}, uint8_t** @code{data}, bool @code{flip})
  This function allows to load TGA image from memory image, pointed by
  @var{raw_data}. Size of the buffer is passed through @var{length} argument
  in bytes. After successful loading of the image @var{header} will contain
  header of the TGA file with full image description, @var{data} will point
  to image array, and @code{TGA_NO_ERROR} will be returned.
  
  You should not allocate memory for image array, pointed by @var{data}.
  Function do this automatically. Image will be loaded from upper left corner
  in any case of image origin position. To flip it vertically, just pass
  @code{true} as @var{flip} argument.

  Use @code{FreeTGA} to free any data, pointed by @var{data} argument after
  successful image loading.
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun tga_error_t LoadTGAFromFile (const char* @code{file_name}, tga_header_t* @code{header}, uint8_t** @code{data}, bool @code{flip})
  This function allows to load TGA image from file and works same as
  @code{LoadTGAFromArray} function.
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun void FreeTGA (uint8_t** @code{data})
  This function free memory, previously allocated by @code{LoadTGAFromArray} or
  @code{LoadTGAFromFile}. Just pass pointer to the @var{data} array.
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun tga_error_t SaveTGA (unsigned int @code{width}, unsigned int @code{height}, unsigned int @code{bpp}, const uint8_t* @code{data}, const char* @code{file_name})
  This function is used to save any pixel array to the TGA file. All you have
  to do is determine size of the image (@var{width} and @var{height}), pixel
  size in bytes @var{bpp} (can be 1, 2, 3 or 4), provide data array in
  @var{data} argument and determine output file by it's @var{file_name}.

  If argument @var{bpp} is out of range, or @var{data} is zero, or @var{width}
  or @var{height} is zero, @code{SaveTGA} will return
  @code{TGA_ERROR_BAD_ARGUMENT} error.
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun void TGALoaderVersion (char* @code{str}, size_t @code{n})
@code{PNGLoaderVersion} function extract module version in @samp{N.N.N.N} form,
where N is a number of version component. Version string will be copied into
@var{str} with null symbol at the end. To prevent buffer overflow @var{n}
argument must contain length of the buffer. Version strings are typically short
(for example @samp{0.2.0.1}); callers should pass the buffer length in @var{n}
to avoid overflow.
@end deftypefun

